nd  nothing no side of the elusive scp with  no idea where it was viola went into the  kitchen she figured she might as well  see if there was anything to eat in this  place maybe it had already gone she  thought she'd have to check in with bass  and see if the tracking tag was still  active at this location this thing could  teleport after all it could be  sunbathing in cancun by now drinking a  pina colada out of a coconut with a tiny  umbrella oh wouldn't that be the life  viola approached the refrigerator and  casually placed her hand on the door  with no idea what was waiting for her  inside she pulled it open and was  immediately hit in the face with a  pillow it wasn't traveling at any  substantial speed in fact it was like  having been lightly thrown by a human  hand more than anything else it didn't  knock field agent smithy back or send  her reeling or have enough force to  cause any injury instead the pillow just  softly impacted viola's face giving a  little squeak like a dog toy would  before it lazily fell onto the kitchen  floor fixed to one side of it was a  post-it note with a crudely drawn face  that glared up at her with a jagged  frown vial aside mildly annoyed that she  just had a pillow thrown at her now  after having spent half an hour  searching the house leaning down she  picked it up and radioed the foundation  she'd found scp-3832  but it didn't end there oh no  after they got the anomaly safely back  in its containment locker it wasn't long  before the foundation was soon inundated  with more pillowy pandemonium nobody was  safe from being the next victim of a  sudden ambush by scp-3832  not even a harmless unassuming  researcher like dr franklin prangley he  had just been going about his day  checking containment procedures were all  in place running a few tests on a few  scps the usual stuff for a scientist  working at site 64. that's when the call  went out over the com system it had  happened again  scp-3832 had vanished from the lock